<header><p class="st-kicker">sultanate · Maritime Southeast Asia</p><h1 class="st-title">Indragiri Sultanate</h1><p class="st-meta">1298 CE – 1945 CE (approx.) · capital Rengat</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">A Malay sultanate on the Indragiri River in Riau, Sumatra, that traded pepper and survived under Dutch rule until 1945.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>Indragiri's early history is known mostly from local tradition, which dates its founding to 1298 and links its first rulers with the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/minangkabau-people">Minangkabau</a> highlands and the Malay courts of the Strait. Its centre lay on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/indragiri-river">Indragiri River</a>, which carried <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pepper">pepper</a> and gold from the interior to the sea, with the court eventually settling at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rengat">Rengat</a>.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>Indragiri was a river state whose rulers taxed trade between the upland <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/minangkabau-people">Minangkabau</a> and the coast. It came under the influence of the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/malacca-sultanate">Malacca Sultanate</a> and later the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/johor-sultanate">Johor Sultanate</a>, and in the 17th century made <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pepper">pepper</a> contracts with the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/dutch-east-india-company-territories">Dutch East India Company</a>. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/islam">Islam</a> was established at court by the 15th century.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dutch">Dutch</a> extended control in the 19th century, signing treaties that left the sultan a figurehead. The sultanate lasted until Indonesian independence in 1945, after which its lands became <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/indragiri-hulu-regency">Indragiri Hulu</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/indragiri-hilir-regency">Indragiri Hilir</a> regencies in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/riau">Riau</a> province.</p><p class="st-conf">Few sources survive for this state; details are uncertain.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><div class="st-emblem" role="img" aria-label="sultanate, 1298 CE – 1945 CE (approx.)"><svg viewBox="0 0 100 100" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M24 82 V62 Q24 40 50 34 Q76 40 76 62 V82 Z"/><path d="M50 34 V24"/><path d="M53 13 A6 6 0 1 0 53 25 A4.5 4.5 0 1 1 53 13"/><path d="M38 82 V66 Q44 58 50 66 V82"/></svg><p class="st-emblem-type">sultanate</p><p class="st-emblem-region">Maritime Southeast Asia</p><div class="st-span" aria-hidden="true"><span class="st-span-bar" style="left:85.53%;width:12.88%"></span></div><div class="st-span-axis" aria-hidden="true"><span>3000 BCE</span><span>1 CE</span><span>2000</span></div></div><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1298 CE – 1945 CE (approx.)</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/13th-century">13th century</a> – <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>sultanate</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>feudal</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Rengat</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Sunni Islam</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Malay</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/indonesia">Indonesia</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Inderagiri, Sultanate of Indragiri</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1622&amp;focus=indragiri-sultanate" aria-label="Indragiri Sultanate on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="7528 2192 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Indragiri Sultanate lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M7848 2448L7959 2663M7848 2448L7959 2664"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M7959 2663h0M7959 2664h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M7848 2448h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M7848 2448h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks Rengat. <a href="/atlas?year=1622&amp;focus=indragiri-sultanate">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
